    },
    {
      "name": "UDP Reference",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Plain-Text Commands",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Documentation only: send ASCII packets to udp://{{udpHost}}:{{udpPort}} using netcat or a similar tool. Commands are case-insensitive.\n\nQuick reference:\n- STATUS -> replies with \"OK playing=<0/1> current=<name> port=<port>\"\n- PLAY <file> [loop=on] [fade=0.5] [fade_out=1.0]\n- STOP [seconds] / PAUSE / RESUME\n- NEXT | PREV | SET <index> | JUMP <track>\n- LOOP <state> (on/off/1/0/true/false)\n- DISPLAY <spec> (e.g. 1920x1080@60 or width=1920 height=1080 refresh=60)\n- FORCE_720P [options] for the 1280x720 preset\n- FASTSTART <file> and FASTGO [seconds]\n- PLAYLIST APPLY items=a.mp4,b.mp4 [loop=on]\n- PLAYLIST STATUS (or INFO) -> returns JSON\n- AUTOPLAY <state> [delay=sec] [restart=off]\n- BRIGHTNESS <value> <seconds>\n- SPLASH_SHOW [text] / SPLASH_HIDE\n\nSee UDP_API.md for the full command matrix and response details.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/udp/docs/plain",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "udp",
                "docs",
                "plain"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "JSON Commands",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Documentation only: UDP JSON packets are UTF-8 objects with a \"cmd\" key and optional \"in_time\" (seconds delay or epoch). Send them to udp://{{udpHost}}:{{udpPort}}.\n\nQuick reference:\n- time -> responds with {ok,t0,t1,t2}\n- play {filename/path, loop, fade_in_seconds, fade_out_seconds}\n- pause / resume / stop {seconds}\n- next / prev / jump {index} / jump_track {n}\n- loop {on}\n- brightness {value, seconds}\n- go_to_start (or goto_start / rewind)\n- startup {macs?, broadcast?, port?}\n- splash_show {text?} / splash_hide\n- shutdown\n\nSee UDP_API.md for payload examples and optional fields.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/udp/docs/json",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "udp",
                "docs",
                "json"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
